OVERVIEW: Create the AVD when missing (installing its system image first) and
boot it. stdout is the serial, or the AVD name with --no-boot.

USAGE: grantiva emulator ensure [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--name <name>] [--system-image <system-image>] [--boot] [--no-boot] [--headless]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --name <name>           AVD name. Defaults to emulator in
                          grantiva-android.yml.
  --system-image <system-image>
                          System image package for a new AVD, e.g.
                          "system-images;android-35;google_apis;arm64-v8a".
                          Defaults to system_image in grantiva-android.yml,
                          then that value.
  --boot/--no-boot        Boot the emulator and wait for it to be ready. On by
                          default; --no-boot creates it without booting.
                          (default: --boot)
  --headless              Boot without a window.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

